n### \uD83D\uDD0D Root Cause\n\nAn **IP pool range overlap** between two LNETs is blocking deletion of an orphaned NIC:\n\n1. Cluster was deployed with **Azure Local 2512**, and \u0060LNET1-Static\u0060 was created with IP range including \u006010.10.35.52\u201310.10.35.61\u0060.\n2. After upgrading to **version 2601**, a new infrastructure LNET (\u0060ceo-clu001-Infra-LNET\u0060) was automatically created with an **overlapping IP range**.\n3. When attempting to delete the orphaned NIC \u0060arcvm001-NIC\u0060 (leftover after VM \u0060arcvm001\u0060 was deleted), the **createupdatevalidationwebhook** rejects the operation:\n   \u003E *\u0022The following IP Pool ranges you entered are already in use: [10.10.35.52, 10.10.35.61] by ceo-clu001-InfraLNET. Please choose different ranges to avoid conflicts.\u0022*\n\nThe webhook validates the NIC against LNET IP ranges, and since the infrastructure LNET now claims those IPs, the delete operation is incorrectly treated as an update/create that conflicts.\n\n---\n\n### \uD83D\uDCA5 Impact\n\n- **Low severity** \u2014 internal test stamp only, no production workloads affected.\n- Customer is **blocked from completing resource cleanup** (cannot delete the orphaned NIC \u0060arcvm001-NIC\u0060).\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Immediate workaround** \u2014 Bypass the validation webhook for the delete operation. Since \u0060arcvm001\u0060 is already deleted, the NIC is truly orphaned and shouldn\u0027t be subject to IP conflict validation on deletion. The Arc Managed VMs team should investigate whether the webhook can exempt delete-only operations.\n\n2. **Direct fix** \u2014 Have the team manually remove the orphaned NIC resource from the ARM/HCI resource store directly (bypassing the webhook), since it has no parent VM.\n\n3. **Resolve the IP overlap** \u2014 After cleanup, reconcile the IP pool ranges between \u0060LNET1-Static\u0060 and \u0060ceo-clu001-Infra-LNET\u0060 to prevent future conflicts. The infrastructure LNET created on upgrade should not claim IPs already allocated to user LNETs.\n\n4. **Bug investigation** \u2014 The 2601 upgrade creating an infra-LNET that overlaps pre-existing user LNET IP ranges is likely a bug in the upgrade path. File a separate bug to track this upgrade behavior.\n\n5. **Escalation** \u2014 Since USGOVVirginia logs are inaccessible directly, the team will need to coordinate with the stamp team or use an authorized path to pull diagnostic logs.\n\n[OUTPUT:incidentFolder] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\n[OUTPUT:summary.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\summary.md\n[OUTPUT:discussion.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\discussion.md\n[OUTPUT:rca.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\rca.md\n[OUTPUT:metadata.md] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\metadata.md\n[OUTPUT:ai_summary.md]","ai.success":true,"ai.model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","ai.durationMs":78768,"ai.inputTokens":225679,"ai.outputTokens":1974,"incidentFolder":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773","summary.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\summary.md","discussion.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\discussion.md","rca.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\rca.md","metadata.md":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\metadata.md"},"globalVariables":{"maxQueryScore":0,"body.timestamp":"2026-04-25T00:35:18.377Z","codeIssueFile":"","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 783872773,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-25T00:35:18.377Z\u0022\n}","repoMdFile":"E:\\work\\hub\\docs\\wiki\\repos.md","body.incidentId":783872773,"rcaFile":"","metadataFile":"","body.serviceName":"","discussionFile":"","mitigationStepsFile":"","body.teamName":"","rootRepoFolder":"E:\\work","incidentId":0